# A cycle that hides behind nullable symbols: S -> A S B is not a unit production,
# but A and B can vanish (A -> ε, B -> ε), so S ⇒ A S B ⇒+ S. The string x then has
# infinitely many trees: S ⇒ x, S ⇒ A S B ⇒ S ⇒ x, and so on.
# Compare with G0: Pasos -> Pasos Pasos is not a cycle, because Pasos is not nullable.
# Try it with: npm run sabueso -- cycles --grammar-file examples/grammars/hidden-cycle.grammar --graph
S -> A S B | 'x'
A -> ε | 'a'
B -> ε | 'b'
